# ─── Per-file targeted exclusions ────────────────────────────────────────
# apps/services/audit-service/src/persistence.py — queries the audit log
# archive. Semgrep's asyncpg-sqli rule repeatedly re-targets different
# lines in the multi-line call expression (433 → 428 → 429 → 438 → 440
# → 452 → 451 → …) as the file is refactored, so per-line `# nosemgrep`
# is unworkable here. All injection surfaces are covered by:
#   * An `_ALLOWED_FILTER_COLUMNS` allowlist in `_build_where()` — the
#     only non-literal interpolated into the SQL is a column-name drawn
#     from this tuple.
#   * Every user-supplied value is bound via asyncpg `$N` placeholders
#     (`tenant_id`, `*extra`, `skip`, `limit`).
#   * Tenant isolation enforced by PostgreSQL RLS + `SET LOCAL
#     app.current_tenant_id` inside the transaction.
#   * Bandit `# nosec B608` retained on each SQL assignment for the
#     same rationale, and Bandit re-runs on every PR.
apps/services/audit-service/src/persistence.py